# Building apps for AgentUI

An **app** is a small web application you write (React frontend + optional backend) that appears in the **Apps** tab of AgentUI. It runs inside AgentUI, uses its look and feel, and its data lives on the AgentUI server. Use it when the user wants a persistent tool (tracker, dashboard, list, calculator, small game…) rather than a one-off answer — for a one-off chart or table, use the `agentui_chart` / `agentui_table` widgets instead.

## Workflow

1. `agentui_app_create` — `id` (lowercase, digits, dashes, e.g. `habit-tracker`), `name`, `icon`, `description`.
2. `agentui_app_write` — send all the files (several per call). The result tells you if the build succeeded; on `ok: false` read `errors` (file, line), fix, write again. The last working version stays online meanwhile.
3. Tell the user the app is in the **Apps** tab (link: `/apps/<id>`). The app updates live for anyone who has it open.
4. Iterate: `agentui_app_read` / `agentui_app_list` to see what exists, `agentui_app_data` to read or push data (see below), `agentui_app_logs` to see `console.log` output and backend errors, `agentui_app_delete_file`, `agentui_app_remove` (only on the user's request).

Icons for `icon`: apps, checklist, chart, calendar, notes, timer, shopping, finance, home, star, book, fitness, music, code, map, mail, photo, game, food, travel, weather, idea, health, tools.

## Files

```
src/main.tsx        REQUIRED — default-exports the root React component
src/*.tsx|ts|css    any other module (relative imports, `import './styles.css'`)
server/<route>.js   optional backend (flat folder, .js or .ts)
```

Limits: 80 files, 512 KB per file, 4 MB total. Only `src/` and `server/` paths are accepted.

## Frontend

React 18 (automatic JSX runtime, no need to import React). Import everything from the provided modules — **there is no npm install**; other packages are not available:

- `react`, `react-dom/client`
- `@agentui/ui` — the UI kit and helpers below
- `chart.js` / `chart.js/auto` — for custom charts

```tsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import { Page, Card, Stack, Row, Text, Button, TextField, List, ListItem, IconButton, Spinner, EmptyState, Alert, useApi, api, toast } from '@agentui/ui';

type Todo = { id: string; title: string; done: boolean };

export default function App() {
  const todos = useApi<Todo[]>('todos');
  const [title, setTitle] = useState('');
  const add = async () => {
    if (!title.trim()) return;
    await api.post('todos', { title });
    setTitle('');
    todos.reload();
  };
  return (
    <Page title="Todos">
      <Stack>
        <Row><TextField style={{ flex: 1 }} placeholder="New task" value={title} onChange={setTitle} onEnter={add} /><Button icon="add" onClick={add}>Add</Button></Row>
        {todos.loading && <Spinner center />}
        {todos.error && <Alert severity="error">{todos.error.message}</Alert>}
        {todos.data?.length === 0 && <EmptyState icon="checklist" title="Nothing to do" />}
        <Card padding={4}>
          <List>{todos.data?.map((t) => (
            <ListItem key={t.id} primary={t.title} trailing={<IconButton icon="delete" label="Delete" onClick={async () => { await api.delete(`todos/${t.id}`); todos.reload(); }} />} />
          ))}</List>
        </Card>
      </Stack>
    </Page>
  );
}
```

### Components (`@agentui/ui`)

| Component | Props |
|---|---|
| `Page` | `title?`, `actions?`, `maxWidth?` (default 860) — scrollable page with header. Use it as the root. |
| `Stack`, `Row` | `gap` (px, default 12), `align`, `justify`, `wrap`, `style`. `Row` = horizontal, centered. |
| `Card` | `padding?`, `onClick?` |
| `Text` | `variant`: `h5` `h6` `subtitle` `body` `caption` `overline`; `muted?`, `mono?` |
| `Divider` | |
| `Button` | `variant`: `contained`(default) `outlined` `text`; `color`: `primary` `danger` `neutral`; `size`: `small`; `icon?`; `loading?`; plus native button props |
| `IconButton` | `icon`, `label` (required, accessibility), `active?`, `onClick` |
| `Icon` | `name`, `size?` |
| `TextField` | `value`, `onChange(value: string)`, `label?`, `helperText?`, `error?`, `multiline?`, `rows?`, `type?`, `placeholder?`, `onEnter?` |
| `Select` | `value`, `onChange(value)`, `options: (string \| {value,label})[]`, `label?` |
| `Checkbox`, `Switch` | `checked`, `onChange(boolean)`, `label?` |
| `List`, `ListItem` | `primary`, `secondary?`, `leading?`, `trailing?`, `onClick?`, `selected?` |
| `Table` | `columns: {key,label,align?,render?(row)}[]`, `rows`, `onRowClick?` |
| `Tabs` | `value`, `onChange`, `tabs: {value,label}[]` |
| `Chip` | `label`, `color?`: `primary` `success` `warning` `danger`; `onDelete?` |
| `Alert` | `severity`: `info` `success` `warning` `error` |
| `Dialog` | `open`, `title?`, `onClose`, `actions?`, children |
| `Spinner` | `center?` |
| `EmptyState` | `icon?`, `title`, `description?`, `action?` |
| `Chart` | `type`: `line` `bar` `doughnut`; `labels: string[]`; `series: {name, data: number[]}[]`; `height?` — themed chart.js |

Icon names (`Icon`, `Button icon`, `IconButton icon`): add, close, check, delete, edit, search, refresh, back, forward, star, heart, info, warning, error, chevron-right, chevron-down, send, download, play, pause, more, home, person, apps, checklist.

Helpers: `toast(message)`; `useTheme()` → `{ mode: 'light'|'dark', lang }`; `useLang()` → `'fr'` / `'en'`… (translate your texts for the user's language); `chartColors()` → palette for custom chart.js charts.

### Backend calls

`api.get(path)`, `api.post(path, body)`, `api.put`, `api.patch`, `api.delete` call **your own backend** (`server/*.js`) — never an external URL. Paths are relative to the app: `api.get('todos')` → `server/todos.js`, `api.get('todos/42')` → `server/todos.js` with `req.path === '/42'`. Failures throw `ApiError` (`message`, `status`). `useApi(path, deps?)` → `{ data, error, loading, reload, setData }` (pass `null` to skip).

### Look and feel — rules

The app must look native. **Use the components above and the CSS variables; never hardcode colors, fonts or radii.** The theme (light/dark) changes at runtime.

- Variables: `--au-bg` (page), `--au-paper` (cards), `--au-raised` (inputs/hover), `--au-accent`, `--au-on-accent`, `--au-text`, `--au-muted`, `--au-line` (borders), `--au-danger`, `--au-success`, `--au-warning`, `--au-info`, `--au-radius` (12px), `--au-radius-sm`, `--au-font`, `--au-mono`.
- Custom CSS goes in a `.css` file imported from a module, referencing those variables: `border: 1px solid var(--au-line); background: var(--au-paper); border-radius: var(--au-radius);`.
- Base font size is 14px; spacing multiples of 4/8px. Mobile first: the app is also used on a phone (≥ 320px wide) — use `wrap`, avoid fixed widths, keep touch targets ≥ 40px.
- The page itself does not scroll: `Page` scrolls internally. Do not use `100vh` tricks; fill the available space.
- No external resources in the frontend (images, fonts, scripts, CDN, direct `fetch` to the internet): the iframe is sandboxed and its CSP blocks them. Use inline SVG or `data:` URLs; fetch external data through `ctx.fetch` in the backend. For live data, refresh with `setInterval` + `api.get(...)` or `useApi`.
- No `localStorage`/cookies (opaque origin): persist through the backend.

## Backend (`server/*.js`)

Each file is a route. Export one function per HTTP method (`GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`); `server/index.js` handles everything no other file matches. Handlers receive `(req, ctx)` and return any JSON-serializable value (or `ctx.status(code, body)`).

```js
// server/todos.js  →  /todos, /todos/<id>
export function GET(req, ctx) {
  const todos = ctx.db.collection('todos');
  if (req.path === '/') return todos.find({}, { sort: '_createdAt' });
  return todos.get(req.path.slice(1)) ?? ctx.status(404, { error: 'Not found' });
}
export function POST(req, ctx) {
  if (!req.body?.title) return ctx.status(400, { error: 'title is required' });
  return ctx.db.collection('todos').insert({ title: String(req.body.title), done: false });
}
export function PATCH(req, ctx) {
  return ctx.db.collection('todos').update(req.path.slice(1), req.body) ?? ctx.status(404, { error: 'Not found' });
}
export function DELETE(req, ctx) {
  ctx.db.collection('todos').remove(req.path.slice(1));
  return { ok: true };
}
```

- `req`: `{ method, path, query, body }` (`path` is relative to the route file: `/` or `/42`; in `server/index.js` it is the whole path).
- `ctx.db.collection(name)` — JSON documents, **synchronous** (no `await` needed): `find(filter?, { limit?, sort?, desc? })` (equality filter on top-level fields), `get(id)`, `insert(doc)` → doc with generated `id`, `_createdAt`, `_updatedAt`; `update(id, patch)` (merge, returns doc or `null`), `remove(id)` → boolean. Collection names: letters/digits/`_`/`-`. Data is private to the app.
- `ctx.kv.get(key)`, `ctx.kv.set(key, value)`, `ctx.kv.delete(key)` — small settings/state.
- From outside the app (cron, your own fetches), `agentui_app_data` reads and writes the same collections and `kv` store; open apps refresh by themselves (`useApi` refetches silently).
- `ctx.user` — `{ id, username }` of the logged-in AgentUI user. All requests are authenticated by AgentUI.
- `ctx.log(...)` / `console.log(...)` — visible with `agentui_app_logs`.
- `await ctx.fetch(url, { method?, headers?, body? })` — calls an external HTTP(S) API from the backend → `{ status, ok, url, headers, text, json() }`. `body` may be an object (sent as JSON) or a string. Public addresses only: localhost, private networks and internal services are refused. Redirects are followed (3 max; `Authorization` is dropped when the origin changes). Limits: 15 s per call, 10 calls per request, 2 MB response. This is the **only** way to reach the internet: the frontend itself cannot (`api.get/post` only reach your own `server/*.js`), so a live-data app fetches in its backend and returns the result.
- Secrets: never write an API key in `src/` (it ships to the browser). Keep it out of the frontend: store it with `ctx.kv.set('apiKey', …)` from a backend route (or ask the user to provide it) and read it in `server/*.js` only.
- Sandbox: plain JavaScript (async/await allowed), no `require`/`import` of modules, no filesystem, no timers, no `eval`. CPU time is limited to 3 s per request (time waiting for the network does not count), 30 s in total. For slow or heavy work, poll from the frontend rather than holding one request open.
- Limits: documents ≤ 256 KB, 20 000 documents per app, responses ≤ 2 MB.

## Checklist before telling the user it is ready

- `src/main.tsx` default-exports the component and the build returned `ok: true`.
- Handles loading, empty and error states (`Spinner`, `EmptyState`, `Alert`).
- Only `@agentui/ui` components / `--au-*` variables for styling; works in light and dark mode and on a narrow screen.
- Texts follow the user's language (`useLang()`), or the language you are talking in.
- Backend validates input and returns `ctx.status(400, …)` on bad requests.
